---
import DocsLayout from "../../components/docs/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "../../components/docs/Code.astro";
import { SOURCE_STEPS, CLI_PATH, INSTALL_SH, RELEASE_TGZ } from "../../data/site";

const build = [...SOURCE_STEPS].join("\n");
const npmTgz = `npm i -g ${RELEASE_TGZ}\ncoding.sh init`;
const env = `CODING_SH_YES=1 sh -c "$(curl -fsSL https://coding.sh/install)"   # no prompt (init --yes)
CODING_SH_VERSION=v0.1.0 ...   # pin a release
CODING_SH_NO_INIT=1 ...        # install only, run init later
CODING_SH_NO_UI=1 ...          # don't open the viewer
CODING_SH_SOURCE=github ...    # skip npm, install the GitHub release tarball`;
const alias = `# from the repository root: put the CLI on your shell
alias coding.sh="node $PWD/${CLI_PATH}"
coding.sh --version`;
const rebuild = `npm run build -w coding.sh   # rebuild only the CLI after a git pull`;
const remove = `coding.sh uninstall --dry-run   # show exactly what would be removed
coding.sh uninstall --yes       # remove coding.sh hooks from every agent
npm uninstall -g coding.sh      # remove the CLI
rm -rf ~/.coding.sh             # optional: delete captured data too`;
---

<DocsLayout>
  <h2 id="one-line">One line</h2>
  <Code code={INSTALL_SH} />
  <p>
    The script checks for Node 22.15+, installs the latest release with <code>npm i -g</code> (from npm once the package is published there, otherwise the GitHub release tarball), runs <code>coding.sh init</code> (it detects your
    agents, shows the plan and asks before writing anything), then opens the viewer. Read it first at <a href="/install">coding.sh/install</a>.
  </p>
  <Code title="options" code={env} />

  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Node.js 22.15 or newer.</strong> The index uses the built-in <code>node:sqlite</code>, and blobs use the built-in zstd in <code>node:zlib</code>, so there are no native dependencies to compile.</li>
    <li><strong>git</strong>, for repository snapshots.</li>
    <li>CI runs on Linux, macOS and Windows. On Windows, run the installer from Git Bash (it comes with <a href="https://gitforwindows.org">Git for Windows</a>). Eval task commands need its <code>sh</code> too. Capture from real agent sessions has not been checked on Windows yet.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="npm">With npm</h2>
  <p>The same release tarball the script installs:</p>
  <Code code={npmTgz} />

  <h2 id="source">From source</h2>
  <Code title="build from source" code={build} />
  <p>The CLI builds to <code>{CLI_PATH}</code>: one file, zero runtime dependencies. Put it on your shell:</p>
  <Code code={alias} />
  <Code code={rebuild} />

  <h2 id="check">Check the install</h2>
  <p>
    <code>coding.sh doctor</code> checks every agent it detects, whether hooks are in place, whether the spool and store are writable, and
    whether the OTLP port is free. Add <code>--json</code> for one machine-readable document.
  </p>
  <Code code="coding.sh doctor" />

  <h2 id="data">Where data lives</h2>
  <p>Everything is under <code>~/.coding.sh</code>. Set <code>CODING_SH_HOME</code> to move it (tests and eval runs do).</p>
  <div class="doc-table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Holds</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>bin/hook.mjs</code></td><td>The hook every agent calls. <code>init</code> copies it here.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>spool/</code></td><td>Raw hook events, one JSON line each, until ingest. Errors go to <code>spool/errors.log</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>index.db</code></td><td>SQLite index: sessions, events, tasks, runs, labels.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>blobs/</code></td><td>Content-addressed, zstd-compressed payloads.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>repos/</code></td><td>Shadow git repositories for snapshots. Your own refs are never touched.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>backups/</code></td><td>A copy of every agent config file before coding.sh edits it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>config.toml</code></td><td>Your config. <code>coding.sh config get</code> prints the effective values.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Set <code>CODING_SH_DISABLE=1</code> in an agent's environment to turn capture off for that process: the hook drains its input and
    writes nothing.
  </p>

  <h2 id="uninstall">Uninstall</h2>
  <Code code={remove} />
  <p><code>uninstall</code> removes only entries coding.sh added and leaves captured data in place.</p>
</DocsLayout>
